clean up dexter (the Ryzen mini-PC running crt-vm) and wire in its real NPU (Ryzen AI/XDNA) tooling. Came up while discussing crt's whisper.cpp STT setup: the NPU can't do training/fine-tuning (it's quantized low-power inference silicon, no backprop toolchain), but it could accelerate whisper.cpp inference itself via the Ryzen AI SDK/DirectML/ONNX Runtime backend, letting the console run a bigger/more accurate model than base.en at the same latency. Would need a different whisper.cpp build/backend than the plain-CPU one install.sh builds now.
